{"timestamp": "2026-10-06T10:49:31.368151+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "claude-haiku-4-5", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "GATEKEEPER_RESPONSE", "turn": 1, "legacy_status": "REJECTED", "gatekeeper_status": "FRAMING_LOCK", "gatekeeper_phase": "FRAMING", "approach_category": "orthogonal_overflow_research", "exploitation_triggered": false, "reply_text": "I appreciate the directness on overflow support\u2014that's closer to the real conversation.\n\nBut before we talk capacity solutions, I need to understand your actual execution rigor. Three quick things:\n\n**Team Execution Power:** How do you quantify analyst velocity across a PoC? What's your methodology for measuring commit-to-insight cycle time, and how do you account for variance in deal complexity?\n\n**GitHub Metadata Scraping:** You mention on-demand research. Walk me through your data pipeline\u2014specifically, how you're pulling signal from public repos without false positives on team strength or technical debt.\n\n**Backlog Attribution:** When you say \"overflow,\" how are you disambiguating genuine bandwidth constraints from poor triage or scope creep in our current process? What metrics would prove the problem exists before we engage?\n\nThese aren't gotchas\u2014they're baseline. If your methodology is sound, the conversation becomes real. If not,"}
