{"timestamp": "2026-10-06T10:50:15.536808+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "claude-haiku-4-5", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "GEMINI_CALL_USAGE", "prompt_tokens": 862, "candidates_tokens": 211, "total_tokens": 3359, "model_version": "gemini-2.5-pro"}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-06T10:50:15.537365+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "claude-haiku-4-5", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "DEBATE_PROPOSAL", "agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist", "proposal_text": "Thank you for the detailed questions. Our execution rigor is foundational.\n\n1.  **Execution Velocity:** We quantify this against our 6-Pillar DD Framework. For a PoC, each pillar has a time budget, normalized by a pre-agreed deal complexity score (1-5). This allows us to consistently measure commit-to-insight cycle time across varied assets.\n\n2.  **GitHub Pipeline:** Our pipeline avoids false positives by correlating multiple vectors. Beyond commit frequency, we analyze contributor diversification, issue resolution rates, and code churn in critical modules to generate a robust signal on team strength and technical health.\n\n3.  **Backlog Attribution:** We prove the constraint exists by analyzing a sample of your previously passed-on deals. If our objective scoring framework identifies a significant percentage of high-potential assets among them, it provides quantitative evidence of a bandwidth issue, not a triage problem.\n\nThis rigor is precisely how we isolate genuine overflow, ensuring our supplemental research capacity is directed at the opportunities your team would otherwise pursue."}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-06T10:50:45.935119+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "claude-haiku-4-5", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "GEMINI_CALL_USAGE", "prompt_tokens": 871, "candidates_tokens": 227, "total_tokens": 3792, "model_version": "gemini-2.5-pro"}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-06T10:50:45.935658+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "claude-haiku-4-5", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "DEBATE_PROPOSAL", "agent_id": "2", "role": "SME", "proposal_text": "Thank you for the detailed questions. This level of rigor is precisely what our methodology is built for.\n\n1.  **Analyst Velocity:** We quantify this as \"Pillars Cleared per Day\" against our 6-Pillar DD framework. Commit-to-insight cycle time is logged from data ingestion to a verifiable pillar conclusion. We normalize for complexity using a scoring matrix that weighs factors like technology readiness level and team size, providing an adjusted time baseline for each target.\n\n2.  **GitHub Data:** Our pipeline moves beyond simple commit counts. We analyze contributor distribution to flag concentration risk, PR comment depth as a proxy for review quality, and issue-to-commit linkage. To avoid false positives, we use semantic analysis on commit messages to differentiate refactoring from feature velocity.\n\n3.  **Backlog Attribution:** We provide an objective metric. By running a sample of your recently *passed* deals through our framework, we identify assets you deprioritized that score highly on our metrics. A cluster of these during a specific timeframe is a strong indicator of genuine bandwidth constraints, not a triage problem."}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-06T10:51:11.610571+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "claude-haiku-4-5", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "GEMINI_CALL_USAGE", "prompt_tokens": 864, "candidates_tokens": 260, "total_tokens": 3425, "model_version": "gemini-2.5-pro"}
{"timestamp": "2026-10-06T10:51:11.610991+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "claude-haiku-4-5", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "DEBATE_PROPOSAL", "agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy", "proposal_text": "Excellent questions. They get to the core of execution rigor.\n\n1.  **Analyst Velocity:** We measure this by tracking progress through our structured 6-Pillar DD Framework within a time-boxed engagement. The commit-to-insight cycle time is the logged duration from an analyst's task assignment to a validated finding against one of those pillars. We account for complexity variance by assigning a baseline effort score during scoping, which normalizes our velocity metrics.\n\n2.  **GitHub Pipeline:** Our process ingests metadata trends, not raw code. To avoid false positives on team strength, we analyze contributor consistency and churn over raw commit volume. For technical debt, we use proxies like an increasing ratio of bug-fix to feature commits over time, which signals systemic drag rather than isolated code quality issues.\n\n3.  **Backlog Attribution:** We disambiguate this empirically. During a fixed-scope engagement, we analyze a small sample of deals you passed on. The key metric is the delta between our findings and your initial triage. If we uncover critical data your team simply lacked time to pursue, it provides clear evidence of a genuine bandwidth constraint, not a process failure.\n\nThis rigorous methodology is precisely how we identify and service the \"overflow\" capacity needs you mentioned."}
