{"timestamp": "2026-10-06T10:53:27.720806+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "claude-haiku-4-5", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "DEBATE_PROPOSAL", "agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist", "proposal_text": "Fair enough. Clarity on the success criteria is the right next step.\n\nHere is our definition for the risk-reversed PoC:\n\nA 'valid finding' is a material, net-new insight, absent from your original diligence files, that quantifiably alters an asset's risk or opportunity profile. This is uncovered using our 6-Pillar DD Framework on the deals you deprioritized.\n\nFor example:\n- **Team Risk:** Identifying a key developer's undisclosed, concurrent project commitment via GitHub metadata analysis, signaling a material risk to execution velocity.\n- **Technical Debt:** Uncovering a pattern of rushed security patches that indicates systemic technical debt, a direct consequence of constrained bandwidth.\n\nThe objective is to empirically test our shared hypothesis: that finite analyst capacity, not a lack of skill, is the root cause of missed signals.\n\nIf these criteria are clear and acceptable, we can schedule the call to finalize the $3,500 PoC."}
