{"timestamp": "2026-10-06T10:53:49.046984+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "claude-haiku-4-5", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "DEBATE_PROPOSAL", "agent_id": "2", "role": "SME", "proposal_text": "Fair request. Clarity is essential for a true empirical test.\n\nHere is our definition: A valid finding constitutes a material, net-new insight, absent from your original diligence file, that quantifiably alters the asset's risk or opportunity profile.\n\nThis is not a subjective measure. Within our 6-Pillar DD Framework, a valid finding would be an objectively verifiable data point such as:\n\n1.  **Technical Risk:** A critical dependency on an unmaintained library, indicating latent security risks your initial scan missed.\n2.  **Team Execution:** A pattern of high contributor churn or a declining bug-fix-to-feature ratio in the core repo, signaling project decay not apparent from surface commit volume.\n3.  **Tokenomics:** An un-audited contract function that permits un-capped minting, directly impacting supply models.\n\nIf we deliver a finding of this caliber\u2014a signal missed due to bandwidth constraints\u2014the PoC is a success. If not, the engagement is at our cost.\n\nDoes this definition meet your standard for clarity?"}
