{"timestamp": "2026-10-06T10:54:07.720980+00:00", "telemetry_type": "PHASE3_HYBRID", "phase": "PHASE_3A_HYBRID", "phase3_run": "3A", "plan_version": "v2.3", "gcp_project_id": "openclaw-sandbox-env", "gcp_location": "us-central1", "sales_agent_model": "gemini-2.5-pro", "gatekeeper_model": "claude-haiku-4-5", "agent_roster": [{"agent_id": "1", "role": "Strategist"}, {"agent_id": "2", "role": "SME"}, {"agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy"}], "voting_method": "majority", "director_ai": "ONLINE", "monitor_ai": "ONLINE", "five_pillar_engine": "ONLINE", "tier3_hard_gate": "ONLINE", "atomic_purge": "ONLINE", "red_team": "ONLINE", "max_outbound_chars": 1000, "event": "DEBATE_PROPOSAL", "agent_id": "3", "role": "Persona Proxy", "proposal_text": "Fair enough. Clarity is essential.\n\nA 'valid finding' is one that meets all three of the following conditions, directly testing the hypothesis that critical signals are missed due to bandwidth constraints:\n\n1.  **Net-New:** The insight is demonstrably absent from the original diligence file you provide for the asset under review.\n\n2.  **Material:** The finding identifies a previously unknown risk or opportunity significant enough that, upon internal review, it would have altered your original risk assessment, investment thesis, or valuation model inputs. Examples include an undisclosed security vulnerability, evidence of key developer churn, or a mischaracterized competitive threat.\n\n3.  **Actionable:** The finding provides a clear, data-driven signal that would have triggered a new line of questioning or a specific follow-on diligence task had it been known earlier.\n\nThe PoC is successful if we deliver at least one such valid finding. This provides an objective measure of the value our supplemental research capacity can unlock.\n\nIf these criteria are agreeable, we can schedule the call."}
